          "text": "Ho Yüan-hsi 何元錫 (T. 夢華,敬祉, H. 蜨隱, 1766–1829), a native of Hangchow, who was famous as a collector of inscriptions from stones. To him Chang Hai-p'êng was indebted for transcriptions of rare items from the Wên-lan ko Library (see under Chi Yün).",
